    "extractedQuestion": "The function ‘t’ which maps temperature in Celsius (C) into temperature in Fahrenheit (F) is defined by t(C)=F where F=(9/5)C+32. Find (i) t(0) (ii) t(28) (iii) t(−10) (iv) the value of C when t(C)=212 (v) the temperature when the Celsius value is equal to the Fahrenheit value.",
    "exactWordingCertified": false,
    "originalPageImageVerified": false,
    "notationRequiresPageImage": true
  },
  "subparts": [
    {
      "id": "g10-ch1-ex1-4-q12-i",
      "part": "i",
      "inputC": 0,
      "answerF": 32,
      "steps": [
        "Use F=(9/5)C+32.",
        "Substitute C=0: F=(9/5)×0+32=32.",
        "Therefore t(0)=32°F."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "g10-ch1-ex1-4-q12-ii",
      "part": "ii",
      "inputC": 28,
      "answerF": 82.4,
      "steps": [
        "Use F=(9/5)C+32.",
        "Substitute C=28: F=252/5+32=50.4+32.",
        "Therefore t(28)=82.4°F."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "g10-ch1-ex1-4-q12-iii",
      "part": "iii",
      "inputC": -10,
      "answerF": 14,
      "steps": [
        "Use F=(9/5)C+32.",
        "Substitute C=−10: F=−18+32.",
        "Therefore t(−10)=14°F."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "g10-ch1-ex1-4-q12-iv",
      "part": "iv",
      "inputF": 212,
      "answerC": 100,
      "steps": [
        "Set F=212 in F=(9/5)C+32.",
        "Subtract 32: 180=(9/5)C.",
        "Multiply by 5/9: C=100°C."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "g10-ch1-ex1-4-q12-v",
      "part": "v",
      "answerC": -40,
      "answerF": -40,
      "steps": [
        "At the same numerical temperature, set F=C.",
        "Solve C=(9/5)C+32; subtract C to obtain 0=(4/5)C+32.",
        "Hence (4/5)C=−32, so C=−40 and F=−40."
      ]
    }
